    "durationMs": 303472,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation** — Go + chi v5.2.1, PostgreSQL via `database/sql` with pgx v5.7.5 (pinned for Go 1.24.3):\n- `main.go` — entrypoint with `migrate` / `serve` subcommands, binds `0.0.0.0:8000`, reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment\n- `store.go` — persistence layer: inserts with unique-violation → 409 mapping, atomic `UPDATE ... clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` for redirects, `count(*) OVER ()` for list totals\n- `handlers.go` — chi routes (`POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`), strict JSON decode (trailing garbage rejected), URL/code validation, JSON `{\"error\": ...}` bodies for 404/409/422\n- `migrations.go` + `migrations/001_init.sql` — embedded migrator with a `schema_migrations` tracking table\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then `exec`s the server in the foreground (binary prebuilt; rebuilds only if missing)\n- `README.md` — start instructions and API reference\n\n**Verified against live Postgres** with a full curl smoke suite: all create/read/list/redirect paths, duplicate-code 409, malformed/missing url and invalid codes (too short/long, bad chars, non-ASCII, empty) → 422, 20 concurrent redirects landing at exactly +20 clicks, and a restart proving links and click counts persist. I also confirmed the exact harness path — `sh start.sh` on a dropped database applies the migration, serves, and returns `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0}` — then stopped the server and reset the DB so grading starts clean.\n\nOne note: pgx's latest release requires Go ≥1.25, so I pinned v5.7.5 to stay compatible with the module's Go 1.24.3 toolchain."
